.TH CONNECT 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
connect \- connect a socket to a peer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/socket.h>
.B int connect(int descriptor, const struct sockaddr* address, socklen_t length);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Connects a socket to an address of the specified byte length.
Linux nonblocking and address\-family semantics apply.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns zero, or \-1 with errno set. Success leaves errno unchanged.
For a nonblocking socket, EINPROGRESS can indicate a pending connection.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR socket (3crunch),
.BR connect (2)
